00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:09.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Junior Team of the Year sponsored by the  Langstone Cliff Hotel Dawlish United  ladies Football Club under 18 on the  back of a hugely successful 2016-17  season  Dawlish United took the leap into  under-18 football the season the girls  had was incredible as they went on to  win another treble of league League Cup  and Devon FA Cups winning 20 out of 22  games to put this achievement into  context they are the only team in Devon  out of over 1,700 teams in youth and  adult football to have won the treble in  each of the past two seasons on top of  the team success there were also four  players selected to play for their  County and another four players selected  for the Exeter City girls Development  Center the success of this team is down  to their incredible hard work and  dedication and was the best possible way  to finish as the girls move on from  youth football Newton Abbot water polo  Under 17's Newton Abbot under-17 water  polo team have had a very successful  year building on previous success in the  2017 season they won the Bristol and  West water polo league junior tournament  and the Devon County under-17 League and  knockout cup they achieved this by  winning every game they played in the  Devon league they scored a hundred and  sixty three goals and conceded  forty-seven and in the Bristol and West  League they scored two hundred and  thirty three conceding 86 the team is  made up of a group of highly dedicated  talented individuals who played  fantastically as a team building on  several years of training and experience  they trained upwards of five hours a  week several doing more members of the  team have played for the county the  region and several of them have been  selected to train with the National  Academy preparing for selection for the  national squads  Southwest underwater hockey under 12s  team Southwest under 12 underwater  hockey team have played and won the  national regions championships as well  as defended their title as national club  under 12 champions the team trained up  to four hours a week and at such a young  age are incredibly dedicated and focused  on their sports they are supportive of  each other  and work effectively as a team they have  a great work ethic and incredible  sportsmanship both of which are key  elements throughout the club the junior  Club has seen incredible growth over the  last 12 months with a club continuing to  go from strength to strength we're all  very excited to see what they can do  next year  [Music]

